    },
    {
      "id": "452edfb734df6b2eef7225ce2f44f5ad533c7af6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 635314389,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The original intention here was to prevent a runaway issue, which occurred during initial development and have an arbitrary limit. Originally we had a counter to prevent an infinite loop. I am ok with removing the limit all together, but this again could lead to an infinite loop scenario.\n\nSo from my point-of-view, this MR is good, removing the limit should lead to additional tests with bad/erroneous config files.\n\n@LarsVoelker just a short question, what kind of profiles do you have that are that big? What is the main reason for those huge files? I am currently preparing further changes for the profile management, and if that requires additional tasks, I would love to recognize them beforehand",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-26T11:10:20.830Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-26T11:11:04.321Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 109477081,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3734,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d1fa1280d2408d00c80592c79e29d442fe0a4f4e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 635582527,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Why I have such large profile files?\n\nMany automotive protocols (SOME/IP, Signal PDUs, ...) are configured quite a bit. For efficiency reasons payloads are not self-describing but payload formats (e.g., parameters of a method call) are configured. With 1000s of parameters and names, etc. configuration items get large.\n\nTypical files that get quite large for me:\n- Signal_PDU_signal_values\n- Signal_PDU_signal_list\n- SOMEIP_parameter_structs\n- SOMEIP_parameter_arrays\n- SOMEIP_parameter_list\n\nbtw, preferences is often 200k already?!",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cccf2084a0438673e9e09f07ed0a5035f6e8815d3d5d888db0023a757c8dce8c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/LarsVoelker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-26T15:25:57.968Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-26T16:51:13.443Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 109477081,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3734,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
